      "DT_ItemLotteryDataTable": {
        "rowStruct": "PalItemLotteryData",
        "fields": 10,
        "rows": 0,
        "source": "paldex-dump+sdk-headers",
        "note": {
          "text": "Row keys here are counters (\"1\", \"2\", \"3\", …) and carry no meaning. What ties an entry to a drop source is the FieldName column, which names a row in DT_FieldLotteryNameDataTable — so searching this table for a lottery name by row key finds nothing. A new drop is a new row under any key the table does not already have (PalSchema's PalRawTableLoader::Apply sends unknown keys to AddRow). Two traps: SlotNo must be a slot the matching DT_FieldLotteryNameDataTable row actually rolls (ItemSlotN_ProbabilityPercent > 0) or the entry can never come out, and WeightInSlot is relative to the other entries sharing that FieldName + SlotNo, so adding one dilutes the existing pool instead of stacking on top of it.",
          "source": "Row keys and the FieldName join: paldex FModel dump of this table. AddRow behaviour: PalSchema src/Loader/PalRawTableLoader.cpp (Apply).",
          "see": "https://github.com/Booyaka101/palschema-hub#lottery-buildings-the-ancient-relic-recycler"
        }
      },
